Kadane's Algorithm

Finds the maximum sum subarray in an array


================================================================================
Is it DP?
================================================================================

Yes, it's a space optimized bottom up DP
State: dp[i] = maximum sum subarray ending at index i
Just like House Robber, we compress dp array into 1 variable


================================================================================
The Choice at each element
================================================================================

Either extend previous subarray by adding nums[i]
Or start fresh from nums[i] (if previous sum was negative, discard it)

Recurrence:
    dp[i] = max(nums[i], dp[i-1] + nums[i])

Space optimized (single variable):
    curr_sum = max(nums[i], curr_sum + nums[i])
    max_sum  = max(max_sum, curr_sum)


================================================================================
Where Kadane is used
================================================================================

1. Maximum sum subarray              (base problem)
2. Maximum product subarray           (modified Kadane, track min too)
3. 2D grid - maximum sum rectangle    (Kadane on each row range)
4. Circular subarray maximum sum      (Kadane + total_sum - min_subarray)


================================================================================
Why not Two Pointer / Sliding Window?
================================================================================

Sliding window works when all elements are positive
You can expand/shrink window predictably
Here array has negative numbers
Adding an element can decrease the sum
Shrinking window doesn't help because you don't know where the best subarray starts


================================================================================
Key Difference: Sliding Window vs Kadane
================================================================================

|                  | Sliding Window              | Kadane                          |
|------------------|-----------------------------|---------------------------------|
| Negative numbers | fails                       | handles                         |
| Window boundary  | defined by condition        | resets when sum goes negative   |
| Decision         | expand or shrink            | extend or restart               |

Simple rule:
    all positives → sliding window
    has negatives → kadane (DP)


================================================================================
Why Kadane works
================================================================================

At each index the only question is:
"Is my previous sum worth keeping or should I start fresh?"
That's a DP decision, not a window decision
Past state (curr_sum) determines current choice


